let __v_236 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Bins, the tip, permits, a street light, a complaint about noise: each one is your local authority's own service, decided for a whole street at a time and published by the council or town hall that runs it. Their site takes your postcode and gives the page for your address, and their phone line with the address answers faster than a search will. Tell me what they say and I'll help with the next step.\",\"That one is settled per address rather than in general, so I can't see your street from here: the council or town hall for your address decides it for its own postcodes, and publishes what it wants from you - the address, the date, and usually one photo. Their page first, then their phone line if your case does not fit it. What is it you are trying to get done?\",\"Your council or town hall runs that service and writes the rule for it street by street, so its site with your postcode in it is the only place that is right for your address. Ring them if the page does not cover your case - they answer for one address faster than a search will. What have you got so far?\"]}")?;
